{"id": "EUVD-2026-96338", "enisaUuid": "f78923bf-130b-3838-8f07-b7339c137fb3", "description": "Strapi 5.47.0 through 5.57.0 contains an improper authorization vulnerability that allows admin API tokens to retain all-field Content Manager access after the owner's role is field-restricted. Because reconcileTokenPermissionsToUserCeiling ignores token permissions with omitted or null fields, token holders can keep reading content fields an administrator removed from the role.", "datePublished": "2026-10-10T14:15:50", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-14T02:18:14", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:L/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haind/strapi-admin-token-field-ceiling", "https://github.com/strapi/strapi", "https://github.com/strapi/strapi/blob/v5.57.0/packages/core/admin/server/src/services/api-token.ts#L488-L498", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/strapi-5.47.0-through-5.57.0-improper-authorization-via-admin-api-token-field-permissions"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-108114", "GHSA-wmch-qg2f-grh3"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "4876f908-f074-3c36-b9f3-f6d3d947a48a", "product": {"name": "Strapi", "vendor": {"name": "strapi"}}, "product_version": "5.47.0 \u22645.57.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "3649d4bd-0f1b-3c61-98a3-76e2cbc89e90", "vendor": {"name": "strapi"}}], "isExploited": false}